    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0782" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg658"/>

                <head>No. 418.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bingham to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Tokei,
                                Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1880-11-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 22, 1880</date>. (Received
                        Dec. 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1209.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg leave to inclose for your information
                    a translation carefully made by Mr. Thompson, interpreter to this legation, of a
                    penal code adopted by this government, and promulgated by his imperial highness
                    Prince Arisugawa Shinwo, acting prime minister of His Majesty the Emperor of
                    Japan, by a proclamation of date the 17th of July last, a translation of which
                    by Mr. Thompson is also inclosed herewith.</p>
                <p>It is to be noted that this code forbids the enactment of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ex post facto</hi> penal laws, and requires that persons shall only be held
                    to answer criminally for the violation of existing laws clearly defining and
                    prohibiting the offense charged.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. A. BINGHAM.</signed></closer>






